Label</p></div><div data-node-id="1262:13358" class="absolute inset-[76.71%_22.38%_23.29%_73.92%]"><div class="absolute inset-[-0.44px_0_0_0]"><img alt="" src="/assets/parity/1130-735-284e3.svg" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="block max-w-none size-full"></div></div><div data-node-id="1262:13359" class="absolute inset-[82.9%_22.38%_17.1%_73.92%]"><div class="absolute inset-[-0.44px_0_0_0]"><img alt="" src="/assets/parity/1130-735-284e3.svg" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="block max-w-none size-full"></div></div><div data-node-id="1262:13360" class="absolute inset-[38.05%_5.23%_61.95%_91.07%]"><div class="absolute inset-[-0.44px_0_0_0]"><img alt="" src="/assets/parity/1130-735-284e3.svg" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="block max-w-none size-full"></div></div><div data-node-id="1262:13361" class="absolute inset-[56.09%_5.23%_43.91%_91.07%]"><div class="absolute inset-[-0.44px_0_0_0]"><img alt="" src="/assets/parity/1130-735-284e3.svg" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="block max-w-none size-full"></div></div><div data-node-id="1262:13362" class="absolute inset-[57.63%_5.23%_42.37%_87.6%]"><div class="absolute inset-[-0.44px_0_0_0]"><img alt="" src="/assets/parity/1130-735-e3b3c.svg" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="block max-w-none size-full"></div></div><div data-node-id="1262:13363" class="absolute inset-[60.1%_5.23%_39.9%_91.07%]"><div class="absolute inset-[-0.44px_0_0_0]"><img alt="" src="/assets/parity/1130-735-284e3.svg" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="block max-w-none size-full"></div></div><div data-node-id="1262:13364" class="absolute inset-[46.88%_5.23%_53.12%_91.07%]"><div class="absolute inset-[-0.44px_0_0_0]"><img alt="" src="/assets/parity/1130-735-284e3.svg" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="block max-w-none size-full"></div></div><div data-node-id="1262:13365" class="absolute inset-[52.36%_5.23%_47.64%_91.07%]"><div class="absolute inset-[-0.44px_0_0_0]"><img alt="" src="/assets/parity/1130-735-284e3.svg" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="block max-w-none size-full"></div></div><div data-node-id="1262:13366" class="absolute inset-[46.88%_22.38%_53.12%_73.92%]"><div class="absolute inset-[-0.44px_0_0_0]"><img alt="" src="/assets/parity/1130-735-284e3.svg" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="block max-w-none size-full"></div></div><div data-node-id="1262:13367" class="absolute inset-[50.5%_22.38%_49.5%_73.92%]"><div class="absolute inset-[-0.44px_0_0_0]"><img alt="" src="/assets/parity/1130-735-284e3.svg" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="block max-w-none size-full"></div></div><div data-node-id="1262:13368" data-name="Note" class="-translate-y-1/2 absolute bg-[#030303] content-stretch flex items-start left-[41.13%] p-[14.212px] right-[46.98%] top-[calc(50%+266.13px)]"><div data-node-id="I1262:13368;265:4711" class="[word-break:break-word] content-stretch flex flex-[1_0_0] flex-col gap-[7.106px] items-start leading-[0] min-w-px not-italic relative self-stretch text-[#ff6b86]"><div data-node-id="I1262:13368;265:4710" class="flex flex-col font-['Space_Mono'] font-bold justify-center relative shrink-0 text-[7.11px] w-full"><p class="leading-[10.659px]">Notes | Account/Orders [Audit]</p></div><div data-node-id="I1262:13368;265:4709" class="font-['Space_Mono'] relative shrink-0 text-[3.16px] w-full whitespace-pre-wrap"><p class="mb-0"><span class="[word-break:break-word] font-['Space_Mono'] leading-[1.6] not-italic">****************<br aria-hidden></span><span class="leading-[1.6]"><br aria-hidden>Information Structure (Crosss Device)</span></p><p class="mb-0"><span class="leading-[1.6]">Imformation heuristics<br aria-hidden></span><span class="[word-break:break-word] font-['Space_Mono'] leading-[1.6] not-italic">Heirachry </span><span class="leading-[1.6]"><br aria-hidden>Type </span><span class="[word-break:break-word] font-['Space_Mono'] leading-[1.6] not-italic">Heuristics</span></p><p class="leading-[1.6] mb-0">Type Roles</p><p class="leading-[1.6] mb-0">Type Sizes</p><p class="leading-[1.6] mb-0">​</p><p class="leading-[1.6] mb-0">****************<br aria-hidden><br aria-hidden></p><p class="leading-[1.6] mb-0">Working through this specific screen (Orders) has highlighted the importance of the need to implement our responsive type system.</p><p class="leading-[1.6] mb-0">​</p><p class="leading-[1.6] mb-0">There are a number of complexities co-exsisiting looking on the current screens, specifically form a rsponsive standpoint.</p><p class="leading-[1.6] mb-0"><br aria-hidden>There are substatntial differences between desktop and mobile tablet and phone. </p><p class="leading-[1.6] mb-0">​</p><p class="leading-[1.6] mb-0">Information is hidden in the smaller devices such as the (Order Summaries). They only appear in desktop. When the breakpoint hits tablet the info disapears, leading me to question is it even relvant.</p><p class="leading-[1.6] mb-0">​</p><p class="leading-[1.6] mb-0">Then there is seemily alot of duplicated information, we could be cleaver and trim it where possible.</p><p class="leading-[1.6] mb-0">​</p><p class="leading-[1.6] mb-0">We Also need to think about the order of information, so for an example when I’m scrolling down the page lets say in desktop, the delivery information and tracking status sits above the Product image and it subset of product order details. In the context of desktop this is not too much of a problem as you are seeing all the information together as the screen can accomodate it.<br aria-hidden><br aria-hidden>The in mobile and tablet the infomation is still stacked in the same manner but becuase the product image is being scaled down to a size so small it becomes less clear as to which order it belongs to. Juts scroll up and down and you’ll see the iussue. <br aria-hidden><br aria-hidden>I think that in a narrow layout constraint, the image should come first, with the delivery status below it, with its subset of buttons.</p><p class="leading-[1.6] mb-0">​</p><p class="leading-[1.6] mb-0">It makes more sense visually as you see the image of what you ordered and then following that cue, you read the information associated with it. Makes much more sense and is far easier to process.</p><p class="leading-[1.6] mb-0">​</p><p class="leading-[1.6]">​</p></div></div></div><div data-node-id="1262:13369" data-name="Note" class="-translate-y-1/2 absolute bg-[#030303] content-stretch flex items-start left-[54.61%] p-[14.212px] right-[33.49%] top-[calc(50%+197.23px)]"><div data-node-id="I1262:13369;265:4711" class="[word-break:break-word] content-stretch flex flex-[1_0_0] flex-col gap-[7.106px] items-start min-w-px not-italic relative self-stretch text-[#bdccf9]"><div data-node-id="I1262:13369;265:4710" class="flex flex-col font-['Space_Mono'] font-bold justify-center leading-[0] relative shrink-0 text-[7.11px] w-full"><p class="leading-[10.659px]">Body</p></div><p data-node-id="I1262:13369;265:4709" class="font-['Space_Mono'] leading-[1.6] relative shrink-0 text-[3.16px] w-full">Body styles are used for longer passages of text in your app. Use typefaces intended for body styles, which are readable at smaller sizes and can be comfortably read in longer passages.</p></div></div><div data-node-id="1262:13370" data-name="Note" class="-translate-y-1/2 absolute bg-[#030303] content-stretch flex items-start left-[54.61%] p-[14.212px] right-[33.49%] top-[calc(50%+53.9px)]"><div data-node-id="I1262:13370;265:4711" class="[word-break:break-word] content-stretch flex flex-[1_0_0] flex-col gap-[7.106px] items-start min-w-px not-italic relative self-stretch text-[#bdccf9]"><div data-node-id="I1262:13370;265:4710" class="flex flex-col font-['Space_Mono'] font-bold justify-center leading-[0] relative shrink-0 text-[7.11px] w-full"><p class="leading-[10.659px]">Titles</p></div><p data-node-id="I1262:13370;265:4709" class="font-['Space_Mono'] leading-[1.6] relative shrink-0 text-[3.16px] w-full">Titles are smaller than headline styles, and should be used for medium-emphasis text that remains relatively short. For example, consider using title styles to divide secondary passages of text or secondary regions of content.</p></div></div><div data-node-id="1262:13371" data-name="Note" class="-translate-y-1/2 absolute bg-[#030303] content-stretch flex items-start left-[54.61%] p-[14.212px] right-[33.49%] top-[calc(50%-193.16px)]"><div data-node-id="I1262:13371;265:4711" class="[word-break:break-word] content-stretch flex flex-[1_0_0] flex-col gap-[7.106px] items-start min-w-px not-italic relative self-stretch text-[#bdccf9]"><div data-node-id="I1262:13371;265:4710" class="flex flex-col font-['Space_Mono'] font-bold justify-center leading-[0] relative shrink-0 text-[7.11px] w-full"><p class="leading-[10.659px]">Display</p></div><p data-node-id="I1262:13371;265:4709" class="font-['Space_Mono'] leading-[1.6] relative shrink-0 text-[3.16px] w-full">Display styles are reserved for short, important text or numerals.</p></div></div><div data-node-id="1262:13372" data-name="Note" class="-translate-y-1/2 absolute bg-[#030303] content-stretch flex items-start left-[54.61%] p-[14.212px] right-[33.49%] top-[calc(50%+352.34px)]"><div data-node-id="I1262:13372;265:4711" class="[word-break:break-word] content-stretch flex flex-[1_0_0] flex-col gap-[7.106px] items-start min-w-px not-italic relative self-stretch text-[#bdccf9]"><div data-node-id="I1262:13372;265:4710" class="flex flex-col font-['Space_Mono'] font-bold justify-center leading-[0] relative shrink-0 text-[7.11px] w-full"><p class="leading-[10.659px]">Label</p></div><p data-node-id="I1262:13372;265:4709" class="font-['Space_Mono'] leading-[1.6] relative shrink-0 text-[3.16px] w-full">Label styles are smaller, utilitarian styles, used for things like the text inside components or for very small text in the content body, such as captions. Buttons, for example, use the label large style or labels on a nav bar.</p></div></div><div data-node-id="1262:13373" data-name="Note" class="-translate-y-1/2 absolute bg-[#030303] content-stretch flex items-start left-[54.61%] p-[14.212px] right-[33.49%] top-[calc(50%-72.46px)]"><div data-node-id="I1262:13373;265:4711" class="[word-break:break-word] content-stretch flex flex-[1_0_0] flex-col gap-[7.106px] items-start min-w-px not-italic relative self-stretch text-[#bdccf9]"><div data-node-id="I1262:13373;265:4710" class="flex flex-col font-['Space_Mono'] font-bold justify-center leading-[0] relative shrink-0 text-[7.11px] w-full"><p class="leading-[10.659px]">Headlines</p></div><p data-node-id="I1262:13373;265:4709" class="font-['Space_Mono'] leading-[1.6] relative shrink-0 text-[3.16px] w-full">Headlines are best-suited for short, high-emphasis text on smaller screens. These styles can be good for marking primary passages of text or important regions of content. </p></div></div><div data-node-id="1262:13374" data-name="Header" class="absolute content-stretch flex flex-col inset-[0_-3.46%_91.11%_-3.68%] items-start"><div data-node-id="1262:13375" data-name="Header bar" class="h-[72px] relative shrink-0 w-[1440px]"><div data-node-id="I1262:13375;4041:275" data-name="Line" class="absolute border-[#e0e0e0] border-b-[0.375px] border-solid h-[72px] left-0 top-0 w-[1440px]"></div><div data-node-id="I1262:13375;4041:278" data-name="Text" class="absolute content-stretch flex h-[15px] items-center justify-center left-[84px] top-[28.5px]"><div data-node-id="I1262:13375;4041:279" data-name="Logo" class="content-stretch flex gap-[6px] items-center relative shrink-0"><div data-node-id="I1262:13375;4041:280" data-name="HTL — Logo" class="h-[10.5px] relative shrink-0 w-[19.523px]"><img alt="" src="/assets/parity/1130-735-410ae.svg" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="absolute block inset-0 max-w-none size-full"></div><div data-node-id="I1262:13375;4041:281" class="flex h-[13.5px] items-center justify-center relative shrink-0 w-0"><div class="flex-none rotate-90"><div data-name="Line" class="h-0 relative w-[13.5px]"><div class